"The patient underwent a robot-assisted radical prostatectomy with a pathological stage of pT2c, Gleason 4+5 (ISUP grade group 5), and positive surgical margins. The seminal vesicles were not invaded, and lymph node metastasis was absent. Biopsy findings showed a progression from Gleason 3+4 to Gleason 4+4.\n\nFactors driving prognosis include the positive surgical margins and the higher Gleason score of 4+5. Countervailing findings include the absence of lymph node metastasis and the lack of extraprostatic extension. The absence of lymph node metastasis is a favorable finding. Missing postoperative PSA or follow-up data widens the uncertainty regarding the subsequent trajectory. The documented prognosis horizon suggests a time frame for recurrence. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and its subsequent trajectory would be crucial in revising this assessment. The fixed estimated horizon is 40.43 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 30.32–50.53 months; its coverage has not been validated."
